<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@/~part_II__cl_7__subsec_2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#subsection> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@/~part_II__cl_7__subsec_2> <https://schema.org/text> "If a power of arrest is attached by virtue of subsection (1), a police officer may arrest without warrant the person against whom the order is made when he has reasonable cause to believe that person is in breach of the order issued under subsection 4(1) or 5(1) or of an order included in a protection order as falls within paragraph 6(l)(a) or (b), by reason of that person's use of violence or, as the case may be, of his entry into any place prohibited under the order."@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@/~part_II__cl_7__subsec_3> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/ontology#has_part> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@/~part_II__cl_7__subsec_3__para_a> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1994/12/eng@> .
